# ICO File Masquerading & Remote Shell – Learning Project

A small cybersecurity experiment I built while learning about file formats, Windows file handling, and remote access concepts.

The project explores disguising a file containing an image as an ICO file and experimenting with the execution of a separate executable (`shell.exe`) when the file is opened.

I used a Windows virtual machine to understand how file masquerading works, how Windows handles different file types, and some of the security risks associated with disguised files.

## What I Used

- **Python** – For scripting and experimenting with the project.
- **ICO Format** – Used as the image file format for the experiment.
- **Windows VM** – For testing file behaviour in an isolated environment.
- **TCP Sockets** – For exploring remote communication.
- **Executable Files (.exe)** – Used to study Windows program execution.
- **Command Shell** – Explored as part of the remote access experiment.

## What I Explored

- Understanding how ICO files work.
- Experimenting with file masquerading techniques.
- Learning about file extensions and file identification.
- Exploring how Windows handles different file formats.
